---
// TEMPORARY demo page — preview at http://localhost:4321/card-demo/ after `bun run dev`.
// Compares card-layout variations for the landing/customization pages.
// FeatureCard.astro has graduated to a permanent, documented component; this scratch
// page is deleted once the Phase 2 introduction/README.mdx landing lands. Demo images
// now live under public/img/ (renamed from the old card-demo-img/ path).
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
import { Card, CardGrid, LinkCard, LinkButton } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";
import FeatureCard from "../components/FeatureCard.astro";
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: "Card Layout Demo", description: "Temporary comparison of Starlight card variations for TomoriBot docs." }}>
  <p>
    Scratch page comparing card styles for the eventual landing page and the
    customization/commands reference. Each section is a different built-in (or
    custom) option, cheapest-effort first.
  </p>

  <h2>A — Built-in icon cards (<code>&lt;CardGrid&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;Card icon&gt;</code>)</h2>
  <p>Zero-effort. Icon + title + text. This is what Starlight’s own docs use. No images — the <code>icon</code> prop is a <em>named</em> icon from Starlight’s set.</p>
  <CardGrid>
    <Card title="Multi-Persona" icon="star">
      Unlimited personas per server, each with its own memory, avatar, and agenda.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Agentic Tools" icon="rocket">
      Web search, reminders, media generation, cross-channel messaging, and more.
    </Card>
    <Card title="SillyTavern Import" icon="puzzle">
      Drop in your <code>.json</code> cards and presets directly via <code>/persona import</code>.
    </Card>
    <Card title="Full Multimodal" icon="open-book">
      Reads and generates images, audio, and video — API or your own local endpoints.
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>B — Link cards (<code>&lt;LinkCard&gt;</code>)</h2>
  <p>The whole card is one big click target. Ideal for the two “how do I get her running” paths on the landing page.</p>
  <CardGrid>
    <LinkCard
      title="Invite TomoriBot"
      description="Try the hosted bot in seconds — no setup. Run /config setup and say her name."
      href="https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=841644102059556915"
    />
    <LinkCard
      title="Self-Host"
      description="Run your own instance for full control over data and API keys."
      href="https://github.com/Bredrumb/TomoriBot#self-hosting"
    />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>C — Action buttons (<code>&lt;LinkButton&gt;</code>)</h2>
  <p>Hero-style call-to-action buttons. <code>primary</code> / <code>secondary</code> / <code>minimal</code> variants.</p>
  <div style="display:flex; gap:0.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center;">
    <LinkButton href="https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=841644102059556915" variant="primary">
      Invite TomoriBot
    </LinkButton>
    <LinkButton href="https://github.com/Bredrumb/TomoriBot#self-hosting" variant="secondary">
      Self-Host
    </LinkButton>
    <LinkButton href="/customization/" variant="minimal" icon="right-arrow" iconPlacement="end">
      Browse commands
    </LinkButton>
  </div>

  <h2>D — Image inside a built-in <code>&lt;Card&gt;</code> (slotted)</h2>
  <p>You can drop a screenshot into a <code>&lt;Card&gt;</code> body. Works, but the image sits inside the card’s default padding/border — a bit boxy.</p>
  <CardGrid>
    <Card title="Multi-Persona Support">
      <img src="/img/3.png" alt="Multi-persona screenshot" style="border-radius:0.4rem; margin:0.5rem 0;" />
      Change personality, behavior, and avatar per server; export as shareable persona cards.
    </Card>
    <Card title="100+ Native Commands">
      <img src="/img/4.png" alt="Commands screenshot" style="border-radius:0.4rem; margin:0.5rem 0;" />
      Everything is managed through Discord’s native slash commands and interactive UI.
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>

  <h2>E — Custom image cards (<code>FeatureCard</code>) — task router into the User Guides</h2>
  <p>
    The landing version: each card is an <em>action</em> (“how do I…”), not a feature brag,
    and links into a User Guide — plus one card into the full commands reference. Image-forward,
    hover lift. <em>(Some hrefs are placeholders for pages not built yet — they’ll 404 in this
    demo; “Connect a provider” points at the existing wiki page so you can see a live link.)</em>
  </p>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <FeatureCard title="Set up multiple personas" img="/img/3.png" href="/user-guides/customization/personas/">
      Create, customize, switch, and export personas — each with its own memory and avatar.
    </FeatureCard>
    <FeatureCard title="Connect a provider" img="/img/1.png" href="/wiki/supported-providers/">
      Bring your own API key or local model: Gemini, OpenRouter, NovelAI, or a custom endpoint.
    </FeatureCard>
    <FeatureCard title="Give her memory" img="/img/2.png" href="/user-guides/customization/memory/">
      Teach her facts, enable RAG documents, and short-term memory across channels.
    </FeatureCard>
    <FeatureCard title="Browse all commands" img="/img/4.png" href="/customization/">
      The comprehensive reference for all 100+ slash commands — the web version of <code>/help</code>.
    </FeatureCard>
  </div>

  <h2>F — Staggered grid (<code>&lt;CardGrid stagger&gt;</code>)</h2>
  <p>Same icon cards as A, but offset for a more dynamic feel.</p>
  <CardGrid stagger>
    <Card title="Memory" icon="approve-check">Long-term, short-term, and per-persona memory.</Card>
    <Card title="Providers" icon="setting">Gemini, OpenRouter, NovelAI, custom, and local models.</Card>
    <Card title="Voice" icon="comment">TTS and STT via ElevenLabs or local endpoints.</Card>
  </CardGrid>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
